{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And if the whole congregation of Israel sin.</b> This is the Sanhedrin, for it is impossible that all Israel would agree to sin. Therefore it says, 'hidden from the eyes of the congregation,' for the Sanhedrin and the prophets and the sages are the eyes of the congregation, as it is written (Isaiah 29:10): 'and He has shut the eyes of you, the prophets' — Scripture explains that their eyes are the prophets. <br>Thus our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: <b>And if the whole congregation of Israel</b> — could it be that Scripture speaks of the entire congregation? It says, 'congregation'; and elsewhere it says (Numbers 35:24): 'and the congregation shall judge.' Just as there it is a court, so too here it is a court. If you say: just as there, the congregation is one of twenty-three, so too here, of twenty-three — it says, 'the whole congregation of Israel': a congregation specially designated for all Israel. And which is that? The Great Sanhedrin that sits in the Chamber of Hewn Stone."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:37.094206648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}